      <section class="info-section">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <h2>Understanding rsync commands</h2>

            <p>
              Rsync efficiently synchronizes files by transferring only the
              differences between source and destination.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="info-grid">
            <article class="info-card">
              <h3>Common rsync options</h3>

              <ul>
                <li><code>-a</code> enables archive mode.</li>
                <li><code>-v</code> displays verbose output.</li>
                <li><code>-z</code> compresses network transfers.</li>
                <li><code>-h</code> displays readable file sizes.</li>
                <li><code>--progress</code> displays transfer progress.</li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <article class="info-card">
              <h3>Safe synchronization</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>
                  Use <code>--dry-run</code> before running destructive
                  synchronization.
                </li>

                <li>
                  Use <code>--delete</code> only after reviewing the preview.
                </li>

                <li>
                  Check the trailing slash on the source directory.
                </li>

                <li>
                  Protect SSH private keys with
                  <code>chmod 600</code>.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <article class="info-card">
              <h3>Common examples</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>
                  <code>rsync -avh source/ destination/</code>
                </li>

                <li>
                  <code>rsync -avz source/ user@host:/backup/</code>
                </li>

                <li>
                  <code>rsync -avz user@host:/data/ ./data/</code>
                </li>

                <li>
                  <code>rsync -avh --delete --dry-run source/ backup/</code>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>
          </div>
